    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "MORNING ONE",
      "narration_text": "The quote for one stock comes back with a price of zero. The workflow reads the price with a JavaScript \"or\", and to JavaScript, zero counts as missing. So it quietly uses the previous close, five hundred and ninety, and the dashboard looks perfectly normal. The math is right. The reader just doesn't know which price they're looking at. I kept that behaviour exactly, because it's the workflow's choice, not mine, and the recipe now notes it for the maintainers. What changed is the record. For every stock, it now says which price was used.",
