    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "THE MORNING IT WAS MY OWN CHECK",
      "narration_text": "And then there was the morning it was my own check. To make sure these checks could actually fail, I broke my own calculation on purpose, and ran the test that's meant to catch it. It passed. All green. But the broken version had never run at all. My test was grading a file left over from the good run. A check that can't fail is worse than no check, because it looks like one. Now the test won't grade anything unless the broken version really ran. And then it catches the break, down to a single cent.",
